<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="Cooked Finance standards for sourcing, safety boundaries, authorship, calculations, updates, corrections, and scalable publishing."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  eyebrow="Editorial standards"
  heading="Useful first. Checkable always."
  lead="A calculator is only as trustworthy as its input definition, assumptions, evidence, and willingness to say what it cannot know."
  updated="August 31, 2026"
>
  <h2>Core standards</h2>
  <ul><li>Answer a real user question rather than manufacture a page for a keyword variation.</li><li>Show formulas, important assumptions, exclusions, and source links.</li><li>Separate standardized test estimates from actual household use.</li><li>Distinguish owner-safe care from work requiring a qualified professional.</li><li>Never invent credentials, testing, first-hand experience, or review.</li></ul>
  <h2>Safety content</h2><p>Safety-sensitive instructions are deliberately conservative. The site does not publish internal electrical, gas, refrigerant, compressor, sealed-system, or pressurized safety-valve repair instructions. A future symptom guide must have a clearly defined observation-only scope and qualified review before publication.</p>
  <h2>Authorship and review</h2><p>Current system pages are published by Cooked Finance and identify their official source set. Organization authorship is not presented as professional certification. When an individual author or reviewer is added, their name, role, relevant experience, and actual contribution will be disclosed.</p>
  <h2>Calculation policy</h2><p>Calculation logic is deterministic, versioned, and regression-tested. We do not hide editorial thresholds behind claims of scientific precision. Repair-versus-replace outputs are scenarios, not predictions.</p>
  <h2>Scaled publishing</h2><p>Structured data can produce consistent pages, but no page should exist only because two keywords can be swapped. Every indexable system page must contain a distinct metric definition, care plan, safety boundary, source panel, and useful connection to the tools.</p>
  <h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>Advertising or commercial relationships may not buy a favorable calculation, conclusion, ranking, hidden link, or removal of accurate criticism. Current content is ad-free.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material factual, mathematical, safety, or source errors are corrected under the <a href="/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a>. Substantive reviews update the page date; silent cosmetic edits do not imply a new review.</p>
